{"name": "paper-figures", "title": "paper-figures", "description": "One study per compositional figure of *A meta-modeler's guide to the cellular interface* (Agmon). Each figure is rebuilt as a process-bigraph composite of DRAFT processes \u2014 typed, unit-bearing ports plus behavior contracts, with no committed mechanism \u2014 and rendered in the paper's visual language alongside the original illustration.\n", "lead": "", "at_a_glance": [{"study": "fig-04", "role": "the cellular interface and its ports (with units)"}, {"study": "fig-05", "role": "cell-environment coupling as a sense/act loop"}, {"study": "fig-06", "role": "disintegration as a grain swap over one interface"}, {"study": "fig-07", "role": "molecular mechanisms and their typed channels"}, {"study": "fig-08", "role": "molecular composition as a nested hierarchy"}, {"study": "fig-09", "role": "self-organization, coarse-graining, autopoiesis"}, {"study": "fig-10-1", "role": "division as a compositional rewrite"}, {"study": "fig-10-2", "role": "development - biofilm reorganization"}, {"study": "fig-10-3", "role": "evolution - variation, selection, new ports"}], "how_to_read": [], "glossary": [], "biological_story": "A cell is modelled from the outside as a bounded, goal-directed system exchanging matter, energy, and information across a small set of interface variables, and from the inside as coupled molecular processes that construct and maintain that interface. The atlas walks this two-sided view: the interface and its ports (Fig 4), how it becomes operational by coupling to environmental fields (Fig 5), what happens when regulation fails and the description drops to molecules (Fig 6-7), how molecular mechanisms compose into nested, self-maintaining organization (Fig 8-9), and how that organization is rewritten across time through division, development, and evolution (Fig 10).\n", "question": "", "hypothesis": "", "object_of_evaluation": null, "status": "planning", "effective_status": "planning", "expert_docs": [], "acceptance_criteria": [], "computed_acceptance": {"verdict_status": "in-progress", "criteria": [], "unmet": []}, "executive": {"what_is_this": "An executable atlas of the compositional figures in *A meta-modeler's guide to the cellular interface* (Agmon). Figures 4-10 are each rebuilt as a process-bigraph composite of DRAFT processes and rendered in the paper's visual language beside the original illustration.", "verdict": "All 11 figure composites build and render; the atlas traces the paper's argument from the cellular interface through cell-environment coupling, disintegration, molecular mechanisms and composition, autopoiesis, and growth -> division / development / evolution.", "verdict_status": "not-yet-run", "decisions_needed": []}, "scientific_argument": {"main_claim": "The paper's recurring composition patterns can be expressed directly as typed process-bigraph composites: interfaces as unit-bearing ports, coupling as shared stores, and shifts in level-of-description as grain swaps and event-driven rewrites - all specifiable as an interface (draft) before any mechanism is committed.", "evidence_for": ["Fig 4 - the cellular interface is a set of typed ports with units (chemical mol/s, mechanical N, electrical A, thermal W, growth 1/hr, viability).", "Fig 5 - cell-environment coupling closes as processes reading/writing shared field stores.", "Fig 6 - one exchange interface is realized by a coarse metabolism process OR a molecular reaction network (grain swap).", "Fig 8 - molecular composition is a nested place-graph of compartments with processes wired to leaves.", "Fig 9 - mutual closure of metabolism, containment, and replication expresses autopoiesis.", "Fig 10 - division, biofilm development, and evolution are compositional rewrites (state partition, hierarchical embedding, port addition)."], "caveats": ["Figures are conceptual: draft processes declare ports + behavior contracts with NO update dynamics, so studies render/structure-check rather than simulate."]}, "references": [], "proposed_inputs": {}, "studies": [{"name": "fig-04", "status": "planned", "effective_status": "planned", "phase": "Design", "title": null, "question": "", "n_variants": 0, "n_interventions": 0, "n_runs": 0, "baseline_source": "viva_meta_modelers_guide:fig04a-interaction-modalities (+1 more)", "parent_studies": [], "n_behaviors": 0, "n_readouts": 0, "n_requirements": 0, "n_followups": 0, "follow_up_studies": [], "discovery_implications": {}, "n_findings": 0, "findings": [], "claim": null, "confidence": null, "design_status": null, "implementation_status": null, "simulation_status": null, "evaluation_status": null, "gate_status": null, "expert_review_status": null, "computed_gate_verdict": null, "derived": {"conclusion_verdicts": {"biological_validation": {"result": "PENDING", "basis": ""}, "regression_compatibility": {"result": "PENDING", "basis": ""}, "explanatory_gain": {"result": "GAP", "basis": ""}}, "verdict": "", "insight": "", "key_metrics": []}, "run_commands": {"baseline": "vwb run study fig-04", "variants": [], "simulations": [], "rerun_hint": "vwb rerun <run-id>"}}, {"name": "fig-05", "status": "planned", "effective_status": "planned", "phase": "Design", "title": null, "question": "", "n_variants": 0, "n_interventions": 0, "n_runs": 0, "baseline_source": "viva_meta_modelers_guide:fig05-cell-environment", "parent_studies": [], "n_behaviors": 0, "n_readouts": 0, "n_requirements": 0, "n_followups": 0, "follow_up_studies": [], "discovery_implications": {}, "n_findings": 0, "findings": [], "claim": null, "confidence": null, "design_status": null, "implementation_status": null, "simulation_status": null, "evaluation_status": null, "gate_status": null, "expert_review_status": null, "computed_gate_verdict": null, "derived": {"conclusion_verdicts": {"biological_validation": {"result": "PENDING", "basis": ""}, "regression_compatibility": {"result": "PENDING", "basis": ""}, "explanatory_gain": {"result": "GAP", "basis": ""}},